<h3>3.3 Key Post-Run Scientific Diagnosis (Why <code>verdict = negative</code> Is Preserved Without Retuning)</h3>
<ol>
<li><strong>Genuine Walker Lane &amp; Piedmont Breakthrough:</strong> Where 1 m LiDAR is present (<code>92.9%</code> in Q3), <code>H1_MULTI</code> <strong>beat <code>REF_H31X</code> (<code>0.1726 vs 0.1602</code>)</strong>, and across the entire survey <code>H1_MULTI</code> boosted low-slope piedmont (<code>&lt;= 6°</code>) off-catalogue <code>SGMC</code> discovery <strong><code>+28.1%</code> over <code>REF_H31X</code> (<code>0.0569 vs 0.0444</code>)</strong> while maintaining <strong><code>&lt;= 58.47%</code></strong> 3-px dot overlap with every single detector raster in the 417-raster registry (<code>39.74%</code> vs <code>GEMSDOE32</code> <code>0.2778</code>).</li>
<li><strong>Exact Cause of Quadrant-1 Deficit:</strong> <code>47.4%</code> of Quadrant 1 has <code>lidar_valid == 0</code>, starving Q1 of dots (<code>3,296</code> vs <code>9,823</code>) when <code>r_lidar</code> enters an un-normalized global sum; additionally, <code>Band 12 det_elev</code> has negative high-pass troughs at steep range-front toes. Per Protocol Rules 5 &amp; 6 (<code>budget = 3</code> experiments, zero post-holdout retuning), we preserve the honest <code>verdict: "negative"</code> receipt and document the exact 2-line sensor-availability quantile fix for <code>KANLER-H1.1</code>.</li>
</ol></article></div></main><footer><div class="wrap"><span>GEMS Evidence Lab &nbsp; / &nbsp; Maximize P(Win) · Own the Outcome</span><span>Research snapshot · No competition slot spent</span></div></footer>
